  "decisions": [
    "Transparent Prover/Verifier is not a private payment route. Actual ZKProver/ZKVerifier wrapper is a separate source construction, not adopted or granted security by its name.",
    "Bare IOP verification returns pending wiring claim. Correct higher entry checks that claim and finishes channels. Generic serialized verifier/constraint system must not be peer authority.",
    "Actual wrapped setup builds outer verifier constraints and a single combined opening schedule. Full same-source and transcript/masking correspondence remains before acceptance.",
    "No identity embedding of all wordAND operations as field multiplication: all words idempotent, fields only0/1. Separate constrained encodings are not ruled out.",
    "Full KEM/KDF/GCM/MLDSA/note/private-state joins, practical recipient completion/refusal and exact whole resources/parser/security remain required. No primitive/profile/cap substitution."
  ],
